  "worked_solution": "The mass $M$ of a plate that occupies the region $D={(x,y)\\,:\\,{e}^{2}\\le x\\le {e}^{6},\\,0\\le y\\le 3}$ with mass density $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ={\u222c}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{D}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x}\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{6}}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{6}}\\frac{{y}^{3}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}[{\\int }_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{6}}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}[\\operatorname{ln}\u2061x]_{{e}^{2}}^{{e}^{6}}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{y}^{3}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{e}^{6}-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061{e}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}4{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y & =[{y}^{4}]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & ={3}^{4}-(0)^{4} \\\\  & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the plate is $M=81.$",
